WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:12.220
What is this?
-It looks the same on the stomach.

2
00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:13.763
Shoulders, head and blood.

3
00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.140
MURDER OF THE CASINO BOSS II

4
00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:16.766
It's my drawing.

5
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.393
Clear.
-They are the same.

6
00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:22.063
The body looks like
down to the gunshot wound in your drawing.

7
00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:24.065
Alright, I'll explain.

8
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:31.156
When Bong-cheon Kim brought me to the casino,
I didn't know how to cook at all.

9
00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:33.450
Why would I know? I was a doctor.

10
00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:37.328
However, I knew human anatomy
excellent already in medicine.

11
00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:42.333
You knew how to handle a knife.
-He suggested that I cook human flesh.

12
00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:44.502
I guessed.
-And not.

13
00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:50.592
Badly indebted gamblers
were brought to me as ingredients.

14
00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:55.430
Did you have to cook human flesh?
-Who ate those foods?

15
00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:56.765
VVIPs.

16
00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:59.184
They went crazy over my food.

17
00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:03.772
Why didn't I get a taste?
I am also a VVIP customer.

18
00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.982
Food was prepared to order.

19
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.568
So the dishes are mentioned
in feedback cards.

20
00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:12.405
The victim sent him a message yesterday
and ordered a special meal.

21
00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:13.948
Made of human flesh?

22
00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:15.950
Did he end up being an ingredient himself?
- For steak.

23
00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:19.204
No. These things are unrelated.

24
00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:23.458
I'm just bitter
because of him my life fell apart.

25
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:27.712
I came up with a recipe to break down
the hatred I feel for him.

26
00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:31.299
In Chef Jang's recipe book
was a drawing

27
00:01:31.382 --> 00:01:35.553
which looked the same
like a victim on stage.

28
00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:38.097
He said he was preparing a special meal.

29
00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:40.850
Perhaps the method of murder was peculiar.

30
00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.854
I think he might
carry out his murder plan.

31
00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.941
In any case, this was a premeditated murder.

32
00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:54.531
The killer had his reasons for taking the body there.

33
00:01:56.574 --> 00:01:58.576
MERIKROTTI JANG'S ROOM WILL BE INVESTIGATED

34
00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:02.705
CONSTABLE HYEON'S NOTEBOOK WILL BE INVESTIGATED

35
00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:13.675
It was mentioned in the constable's notebook
Four season Jeon and Bong-cheon Kim.

36
00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:16.469
It says at the bottom of the page
"city hall archive".

37
00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:19.681
There might be something there. In that case…

38
00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:21.099
WHAT IS HE LOOKING FOR IN THE ARCHIVES?

39
00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:23.351
We are digging places.
- Let's see what's here.

40
00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:24.686
There are a lot of folders.

41
00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.355
Let's go through them all.

42
00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:32.735
Select the folder from the early 2000s,
because the incident happened in 2002.

43
00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:38.950
Lots of folders.

44
00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.038
What is this?
-Wait.

45
00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:46.749
FORCED RELOCATION PLAN OF THE DESTROYED CITY 2002

46
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.502
"City of Destruction."
- Here's a folder about it.

47
00:02:50.753 --> 00:02:51.796
TRANSFER PERMIT FORM

48
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.674
Oops, look what I found.

49
00:02:54.757 --> 00:02:56.718
HEOYOUNG ENVIRONMENTAL REPORT

50
00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.679
Jeweler Ani had a copy of this.

51
00:02:59.762 --> 00:03:01.764
Mass deaths of fish are mentioned here.

52
00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:06.853
Some of those listed in the permit form
of persons has disappeared.

53
00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:09.606
Persons crossed out in red
have disappeared.

54
00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.983
Those who did not give permission disappeared.

55
00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:16.279
Others gave permission and did not disappear.
"Resolute Park, Defiant Han."

56
00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.114
NEXT PAGE OF TRANSFER FORM

57
00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:22.577
Jang the cormorant huh?
-Corkfish?

58
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.163
I guess they're married
because they have the same address.

59
00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:26.915
Jang the cormorant is missing.

60
00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:29.250
Both are missing.
It means something.

61
00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.877
Wait a minute, listen.

62
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.047
If only it wasn't about that
for avenging Constable Hyeon's death?

63
00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.549
Would you forgive the man,
who hurt your wife?

64
00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:37.926
I would kill him.
-Right.

65
00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:43.139
This doesn't show
from the standard license form.

66
00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:48.645
Was Korukauppias involved in this?
in his civil service days?

67
00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.980
Do you remember the deal he made?
- He agreed.

68
00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.149
Now.
-Listen.

69
00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.567
Cormorant.
- Did you find anything?

70
00:03:54.651 --> 00:03:57.737
Mr. Seagull, we want to talk.
-Would you come here?

71
00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.323
You can examine the body later.
- Now what?

72
00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:05.411
Mr. Sea Groat.
Were you married in 2002?

73
00:04:05.495 --> 00:04:07.497
Were you married?
-Married?

74
00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.458
Is it forbidden?
- Where is your wife?

75
00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:14.754
How could I answer that,
when he is no longer in this world?

76
00:04:14.837 --> 00:04:16.047
How did he die?

77
00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:20.260
What do you mean?
-What happened to him?

78
00:04:20.343 --> 00:04:21.844
He died.
-When?

79
00:04:22.637 --> 00:04:23.680
Maybe he killed the wife.

80
00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.433
Don't take it again.

81
00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:28.810
He did it again.

82
00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:31.020
Tell me now, Merikrott.
-What happened to him?

83
00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.897
I think he disappeared in May 2002.

84
00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:36.693
Her name was Wife Lim.
He lived at 79-1 Tuhokaupunki.

85
00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.779
Was that your address?
-It was.

86
00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:41.781
How did you come back in one piece?
-Tell me.

87
00:04:41.864 --> 00:04:46.202
Your wife disappeared and died.
How did you survive?

88
00:04:47.203 --> 00:04:48.288
Take a look...

89
00:04:51.374 --> 00:04:54.502
We were told to move
for compensation.

90
00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:57.880
That's what your father told everyone, wasn't he?

91
00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:04.846
Proposed compensation
however, was shocking.

92
00:05:04.929 --> 00:05:07.348
Not a million won
enough per economy.

93
00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:09.225
An incredible amount.
-True.

94
00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.519
That's why me and my wife…

95
00:05:11.602 --> 00:05:16.566
Sorry.
-We decided to stay in Tuhokaupunki.

96
00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.194
One night…
-What happened?

97
00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:26.200
Men broke into our house,
who abused me and my wife.

98
00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:29.746
Is that what got you scarred?
-Yes.

99
00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.040
Didn't it come from gambling?
-Don't be stupid.

100
00:05:32.123 --> 00:05:34.500
Maybe you scratch your head in your sleep.

101
00:05:35.084 --> 00:05:38.504
Sense the atmosphere.
-Do you want a scar too?

102
00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:44.260
Sense the atmosphere.
- Then I woke up -

103
00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:47.555
buried in a landfill.
-Oh no.

104
00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.017
FOUR SEASONS BY JEON'S ORDER
BONG-CHEON KIM -

105
00:05:51.642 --> 00:05:53.811
YOUR GRAVES REFUSED
AND REPORTED MISSING

106
00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:56.773
When I somehow came to my senses,

107
00:05:56.856 --> 00:06:01.277
I saw my wife lying bloody next to me.

108
00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.864
I tried to wake him up.
I didn't want him to die.

109
00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:07.658
Then I passed out again.

110
00:06:07.742 --> 00:06:10.536
The next thing I woke up from the hospital.

111
00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.790
I asked after my wife
and I asked others to look for him.

112
00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.210
Turns out he was already dead.

113
00:06:18.086 --> 00:06:21.297
Officer Hyeon dug me out of the hole.

114
00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.799
DEAD CONSTABLE HYEON

115
00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:29.013
So you wanted revenge
the death of both your mentor and your wife.

116
00:06:29.097 --> 00:06:30.473
It's a double motive.

117
00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:34.852
Detective, look at this. My parents too
signed the permission form.

118
00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:39.315
Singer Kim's father and mother.

119
00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:42.693
I will tell you something about Laulaja's family.

120
00:06:42.777 --> 00:06:47.532
As a beginner fisherman
prey was hard to come by.

121
00:06:47.615 --> 00:06:53.621
How did you become more skilled?
-One day the water was full of fish.

122
00:06:53.704 --> 00:06:54.705
Right.

123
00:06:54.789 --> 00:06:57.625
I grabbed every single one
and I considered myself lucky.

124
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:00.086
The fish were dead.
- They were.

125
00:07:00.169 --> 00:07:03.005
It never occurred to me,

126
00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:06.217
that the fish were dead
for heavy metal poisoning.

127
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.389
I didn't ask for full price. I sold the fish
cheap, because they were already dead.

128
00:07:11.472 --> 00:07:14.100
You shouldn't have sold them.
-They were contaminated.

129
00:07:14.183 --> 00:07:16.686
I really didn't know that!

130
00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:20.481
What happened to your parents
after the move?

131
00:07:20.565 --> 00:07:24.318
Did they slowly wither to death?
-Yes, both my parents died.

132
00:07:24.402 --> 00:07:28.573
Now that I think about it,
the fish must have died because

133
00:07:28.656 --> 00:07:31.742
that I watched
dumping waste into the sea through the fingers.

134
00:07:31.826 --> 00:07:34.162
The landfill was contaminated
heavy metals,

135
00:07:34.245 --> 00:07:36.497
and therefore the fish also died.
-Apparently.

136
00:07:36.581 --> 00:07:38.332
You were also involved!

137
00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:42.003
I could pay people less,
but did not bury them.

138
00:07:42.086 --> 00:07:43.838
Were you actively involved?

139
00:07:43.921 --> 00:07:46.340
I wasn't.
- Did you know about the burials?

140
00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:47.425
I didn't know.

141
00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:50.094
This needs to be thoroughly investigated.

142
00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:54.474
Everyone is somehow related to the landfill.

143
00:07:54.557 --> 00:07:59.979
It seems to be crucial
find out the connection -

144
00:08:00.062 --> 00:08:03.858
Bong-cheon Kim,
between the dump and the suspects.

145
00:08:04.942 --> 00:08:10.031
Jang the seal for sure
broken and enraged by the death of his wife.

146
00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:14.994
Also his mentor
Constable Hyeon died.

147
00:08:15.077 --> 00:08:19.457
Then he found
Constable Hyeon's notebook -

148
00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:26.172
and saw forced relocation, Bong-cheon Kim and
memoranda concerning the archives of the town hall.

149
00:08:26.255 --> 00:08:29.675
Shouldn't he have started investigating the mess himself?

150
00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:32.762
I'll find out for myself.

151
00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:35.765
HE FOCUSES ON INVESTIGATING
MERIKROTTI JANG'S ROOM

152
00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:45.691
IN THE TRASH BASKET

153
00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:51.072
"Goodbye Asthma"? Inhalable medicine.

154
00:08:52.073 --> 00:08:55.451
For asthma patients. “Breathe in
via nebulizer for ten minutes."

155
00:08:58.079 --> 00:09:00.790
Why did he throw this away
even if the bottle is not empty?

156
00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:03.042
Goodness!

157
00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:06.254
THE OWNER OF THE ROOM SAW HIM

158
00:09:06.337 --> 00:09:09.549
I have asthma.
That's what those drugs are for.

159
00:09:10.341 --> 00:09:12.093
Look.
-Does this go in your mouth?

160
00:09:12.176 --> 00:09:13.219
Yeah, I did.

161
00:09:14.345 --> 00:09:15.388
This is not empty.

162
00:09:15.471 --> 00:09:16.472
HALF FULL

163
00:09:16.556 --> 00:09:17.890
Right?
-No.

164
00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:24.814
I didn't know. Where did you find it?
- From the trash can.

165
00:09:25.815 --> 00:09:27.817
Really? I guess I didn't notice it.

166
00:09:30.194 --> 00:09:32.613
SHE CONTINUES TO EXPLORE MERIKROT'S ROOM

167
00:09:36.617 --> 00:09:39.662
EX-WIFE'S EFFECTS

168
00:09:43.791 --> 00:09:45.001
What is this?

169
00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:49.338
"Medical report, Wife Lim".

170
00:09:50.673 --> 00:09:51.882
"Flu."

171
00:09:53.801 --> 00:09:54.969
"White blood cell count."

172
00:09:55.678 --> 00:09:58.139
I guess there is a recording of his voice?

173
00:09:59.307 --> 00:10:01.350
Mr.
-So?

174
00:10:01.434 --> 00:10:02.977
What is this?
-What do you mean?

175
00:10:05.187 --> 00:10:08.065
It's my wife's doctor's report.
-Why was it hidden?

176
00:10:08.649 --> 00:10:11.152
Should it have been on the bed?
-You hid it.

177
00:10:12.653 --> 00:10:13.988
Why did you hide this?

178
00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:15.656
What now?

179
00:10:16.574 --> 00:10:20.911
A statement about the wife.
-Right. Now I'm starting to remember.

180
00:10:20.995 --> 00:10:22.788
What now?
-Detective.

181
00:10:22.872 --> 00:10:26.208
Now I remember.
-His wife's medical report.

182
00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:29.086
Before his death -

183
00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.674
my wife went to the doctor.
- I guessed.

184
00:10:33.758 --> 00:10:36.010
Come here.
-He's more suspicious.

185
00:10:36.093 --> 00:10:37.928
Who Prescribed Dylenol?

186
00:10:38.012 --> 00:10:39.555
Wait a minute.

187
00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:42.224
Look.
-His doctor was Chef Jang.

188
00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:45.561
I knew the name sounded familiar,
and here's the reason.

189
00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:48.689
I haven't seen this in ages.
-"Samryu University, Neurosurgery."

190
00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:52.401
This was in April 2002
before the May transfer applications.

191
00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:55.780
"The patient complained of constant pain in the limbs.
Blood tests were taken."

192
00:10:55.863 --> 00:10:58.240
"The diagnosis is flu.
Prescribed drug: Dylenol."

193
00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.701
Hello, sir.
-Wait.

194
00:11:00.785 --> 00:11:03.621
You get a chance to kill him.
Your wife died because of him.

195
00:11:03.704 --> 00:11:10.294
I guess he acted at the request of Nelikausi Jeon
and intentionally gave false diagnoses.

196
00:11:10.378 --> 00:11:15.174
During this time he was paid for the wrong
three billion won for diagnoses.

197
00:11:15.716 --> 00:11:17.843
No, you misunderstood.

198
00:11:17.927 --> 00:11:20.554
What we misunderstood,
when the evidence is clear?

199
00:11:20.638 --> 00:11:23.891
It's not as you think.
Nobody asked me for anything.

200
00:11:24.475 --> 00:11:26.394
So you're a bum?
-You misdiagnosed.

201
00:11:26.477 --> 00:11:27.395
Nope.

202
00:11:28.437 --> 00:11:31.232
I made the wrong diagnoses first.
-Without a reason?

203
00:11:31.315 --> 00:11:33.401
Did you ask for money after that?

204
00:11:33.484 --> 00:11:38.614
After making the wrong diagnoses
I took the medical reports to his father.

205
00:11:38.697 --> 00:11:41.659
I offered a solution to his problems.
- Or so.

206
00:11:42.284 --> 00:11:43.452
What "or so"?

207
00:11:44.745 --> 00:11:47.873
We're in the same boat whether you like it or not.

208
00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:49.917
I haven't seen you before today.

209
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.044
Your father was the mayor then.

210
00:11:52.128 --> 00:11:56.757
To weather the storm, it is best to…
- I'll show you how flus are contagious.

211
00:11:56.841 --> 00:11:57.842
Oh no.
-Wait.

212
00:11:57.925 --> 00:12:00.803
I'll show you how flus are contagious.
-Wait.

213
00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:03.055
I'll show you how to get sick.

214
00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:04.765
That's it, shoot him.
-Wait.

215
00:12:04.849 --> 00:12:05.850
Clear.
-Wait.

216
00:12:05.933 --> 00:12:07.935
Wait.
-His father is complicit.

217
00:12:08.018 --> 00:12:11.814
You can all testify how healthy
a grown man gets a cold!

218
00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:14.275
I'll show you!

219
00:12:14.358 --> 00:12:16.944
Listen…
- I'll show you!

220
00:12:17.027 --> 00:12:20.573
Citizens, I apologize
for the deeds of my father.

221
00:12:24.368 --> 00:12:25.453
I would like…

222
00:12:25.536 --> 00:12:26.454
COMPLETE CHAOS

223
00:12:26.537 --> 00:12:29.331
What a mess.
-Mayhem.

224
00:12:29.999 --> 00:12:34.795
I apologize for my father.
However, if I become president…

225
00:12:34.879 --> 00:12:36.881
Really?
-History does not repeat itself.

226
00:12:36.964 --> 00:12:38.841
How can you still dream about it?

227
00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:42.136
It's chaos here.

228
00:12:42.928 --> 00:12:46.515
By selling contaminated fish -

229
00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:49.477
Jang the cormorant exposed the inhabitants
for heavy metals.

230
00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:53.397
His actions compromised
also his wife's life.

231
00:12:53.481 --> 00:12:57.693
If several heavy metals
cases of poisoning would have come to light,

232
00:12:57.776 --> 00:13:02.781
the then mayor
would have lost his political career.

233
00:13:02.865 --> 00:13:05.075
To cover it up, he paid -

234
00:13:05.159 --> 00:13:08.204
to a doctor named Chef Jang
about managing the situation.

235
00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:11.749
In light of the evidence, it is clear.

236
00:13:13.918 --> 00:13:17.379
Where is Mrs. Mayor's phone?
- No information.

237
00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.006
I guess you have a phone?
-There is.

238
00:13:19.089 --> 00:13:20.257
Give it here.
-Anna.

239
00:13:20.799 --> 00:13:23.886
Can't we look at your phone?
- You can. Go ahead.

240
00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:25.221
Does it have secrets?

241
00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:29.850
There isn't. I just don't like your tone of voice.
-What do you mean?

242
00:13:29.934 --> 00:13:34.021
The singer and the cormorant.
-Do you think you are safe as mayor?

243
00:13:34.104 --> 00:13:36.524
I'm not usually involved
with people like you.

244
00:13:36.607 --> 00:13:39.985
You can't treat me like this.
Do you want to go to jail?

245
00:13:40.069 --> 00:13:42.863
He revealed his true nature.
- He doesn't hold back anymore.

246
00:13:42.947 --> 00:13:44.907
Do you want to go to jail? Do you know who I am?

247
00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:48.077
Are you a mayor or a cop?
-Who would want to go to jail?

248
00:13:48.577 --> 00:13:49.912
Be quiet.

249
00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:54.792
This is Bong-cheon Kim.
- Found it.

250
00:13:54.875 --> 00:13:56.585
MAYOR JEON'S PHONE

251
00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:58.295
RECORDING OF THE CALL

252
00:13:58.379 --> 00:13:59.672
Be quiet.

253
00:13:59.755 --> 00:14:01.966
This is Bong-cheon Kim.
- Found it.

254
00:14:02.049 --> 00:14:04.176
Do you want to build a stadium
to the casino area?

255
00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.387
We should have discussed it.

256
00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.389
We can open the vault with it.
- He's angry.

257
00:14:09.807 --> 00:14:13.811
Or discuss?
Don't you know the city owns the lot?

258
00:14:13.894 --> 00:14:18.274
I want to hear too.
-Don't complain, just move your casino. Bye!

259
00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:21.318
THE SECRET VAULT

260
00:14:21.402 --> 00:14:23.862
Madam Mayor.
-Will this work?

261
00:14:24.446 --> 00:14:25.781
This is Bong-cheon Kim.

262
00:14:27.575 --> 00:14:28.576
It opened.

263
00:14:28.659 --> 00:14:30.160
This is Bong-cheon Kim.

264
00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.080
IT OPENED!

265
00:14:33.998 --> 00:14:35.457
It opened.
-Did it work?

266
00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:36.542
For real?
- I knew that.

267
00:14:36.625 --> 00:14:38.043
It worked.
-Who is to blame?

268
00:14:38.127 --> 00:14:39.670
Does it really work?
- I knew it!

269
00:14:39.753 --> 00:14:41.881
THE SECRET VAULT

270
00:14:41.964 --> 00:14:44.508
We're on the trail of the culprit.
-Finally in the vault.

271
00:14:44.592 --> 00:14:45.593
What are all these?

272
00:14:45.676 --> 00:14:47.136
I didn't think it would open the door.

273
00:14:47.761 --> 00:14:49.263
Look!
-I freaked out.

274
00:14:49.346 --> 00:14:50.931
Bullet mark!

275
00:14:51.015 --> 00:14:52.892
DID THE BULLET GO FROM HERE?

276
00:14:52.975 --> 00:14:56.437
There's one here too.
- From a gunshot wound to the head.

277
00:14:57.855 --> 00:15:01.025
This is from a bullet that went through the head.
- Well noticed.

278
00:15:01.108 --> 00:15:03.444
This one was shot in the head, this one in the shoulder.

279
00:15:03.527 --> 00:15:05.070
Pam.
- Two shots.

280
00:15:05.154 --> 00:15:06.697
Two bullet marks.

281
00:15:07.615 --> 00:15:09.491
I see blood.
- There's blood here.

282
00:15:10.326 --> 00:15:12.995
I guess his head was here.
-So.

283
00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:14.955
Wait a minute.
- Now what?

284
00:15:15.039 --> 00:15:20.002
There used to be a carpet here.
When I visited here, there was a carpet on the floor.

285
00:15:20.085 --> 00:15:22.671
The killer dragged the body away on the carpet!

286
00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:25.049
Come to your senses.

287
00:15:25.132 --> 00:15:27.259
Was the body dragged away using a carpet?

288
00:15:27.343 --> 00:15:29.511
Even a woman could do it.
-Easily.

289
00:15:30.137 --> 00:15:32.348
If there is a shooting here...
-The vault is soundproof.

290
00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:35.851
Right.
- Elsewhere, the shots would have been heard.

291
00:15:35.935 --> 00:15:37.811
Glad you remembered that.

292
00:15:37.895 --> 00:15:40.230
Is he the only one who had access here?

293
00:15:41.106 --> 00:15:43.108
I didn't get here.
-He's the only one.

294
00:15:43.192 --> 00:15:44.234
How would I have gotten in?

295
00:15:44.318 --> 00:15:47.112
We got in
with your phone's recording!

296
00:15:47.196 --> 00:15:48.989
I wouldn't have gotten in.
-Listen.

297
00:15:49.073 --> 00:15:51.575
How would I have known
that recording opens the door?

298
00:15:51.659 --> 00:15:52.910
Surely you knew.

299
00:15:52.993 --> 00:15:56.872
Who would have known
that just the recording opens the vault?

300
00:15:56.956 --> 00:16:01.502
The display outside reads,
that the lock works with a voice command.

301
00:16:01.585 --> 00:16:06.715
Someone moved the body from the vault,
be it the Mayor or the Jeweler.

302
00:16:06.799 --> 00:16:12.179
You are here today because someone sent
I invite you by email.

303
00:16:12.262 --> 00:16:15.557
Email sent
after the estimated time of death.

304
00:16:15.641 --> 00:16:16.809
Here…

305
00:16:18.978 --> 00:16:20.604
We are investigating the emails that have been sent.

306
00:16:20.688 --> 00:16:22.439
Were they timed?
-I got mine at 7 o'clock.

307
00:16:22.523 --> 00:16:25.401
See "scheduled emails".
-There must be something there.

308
00:16:25.484 --> 00:16:28.195
They were sent to the Jeweler,
To the Mayor, Merikrot -

309
00:16:28.278 --> 00:16:30.239
For the Chef and the Singer.

310
00:16:30.322 --> 00:16:34.326
They were created on the 7th.
This confirms it. The killer sent them.

311
00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.871
The killer timed the messages.
-On this laptop.

312
00:16:37.955 --> 00:16:40.791
He also sent the information
of the changed date for those

313
00:16:40.874 --> 00:16:43.919
who were originally invited.
- So April 15th.

314
00:16:44.003 --> 00:16:46.672
After murdering the victim -

315
00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:50.509
the killer sent them word,
so that they would not come.

316
00:16:50.592 --> 00:16:52.469
This he sent to the guests.

317
00:16:52.553 --> 00:16:55.305
Here is the original invitation.

318
00:16:55.389 --> 00:16:58.726
They were not offered 100 million won.
We got a coupon worth it.

319
00:16:59.476 --> 00:17:03.188
Our invitations read,
that we could turn the coupon into money.

320
00:17:03.272 --> 00:17:05.107
I guess everyone would do that now?

321
00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:08.360
Even me who doesn't gamble…
- You would still be interested.

322
00:17:08.444 --> 00:17:10.821
Of course.
Yes, a free 100 million won will do.

323
00:17:10.904 --> 00:17:13.157
I was puzzled when I saw it.

324
00:17:13.741 --> 00:17:18.495
I thought maybe the boss wanted to
gives me a bonus and I got excited.

325
00:17:18.579 --> 00:17:20.080
So the killer ran like this,

326
00:17:20.164 --> 00:17:22.916
that the five of you received the email
this morning at seven.

327
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.960
The murder was staged.
-True.

328
00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:30.007
We all had a story to tell.
The killer put it on display for us.

329
00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:34.970
So the killer was looking for all those people,
who bore a grudge against Bong-cheon Kim.

330
00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:40.684
Right.
The killer knows how we relate to him.

331
00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.020
But I…
- Now what?

332
00:17:43.103 --> 00:17:45.731
I didn't guess.
-You had a transfer contract.

333
00:17:46.315 --> 00:17:49.485
You knew his parents.

334
00:17:49.568 --> 00:17:52.237
I didn't have a form.
-His family had to move.

335
00:17:52.321 --> 00:17:54.865
I would have known
if I had the form.

336
00:17:55.532 --> 00:17:56.867
Mrs.
-So?

337
00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:01.872
You can figure it out.
- The mayor has the most information.

338
00:18:01.955 --> 00:18:05.084
Listen up. Let's think
that he will become president.

339
00:18:05.167 --> 00:18:07.294
What if this came out then?

340
00:18:07.377 --> 00:18:10.047
This was like for him
purification ritual.

341
00:18:10.798 --> 00:18:14.760
What did the killer gain from it,
that he brought us here

342
00:18:14.843 --> 00:18:18.639
and we see the body laid out like that?
-What is the killer trying to say?

343
00:18:19.473 --> 00:18:22.184
Maybe he thinks -

344
00:18:22.267 --> 00:18:24.895
to have taken revenge for us.
- Could be.

345
00:18:24.978 --> 00:18:28.899
You mean the killer got his revenge
for all of us?

346
00:18:28.982 --> 00:18:33.028
That's why the body was laid out.
-Who would commit such a selfless murder?

347
00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.241
Why did the killer do this?
- The answer is on stage.

348
00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.160
What's wrong with your lips?

349
00:18:40.244 --> 00:18:41.829
Lips interest me.

350
00:18:42.579 --> 00:18:44.665
What is it?
- Let's investigate.

351
00:18:44.748 --> 00:18:48.168
Can we examine the CEO's body
and find out what's on the lips?

352
00:18:48.252 --> 00:18:50.504
Yeah, let's examine the lips.
- They interest me.

353
00:18:50.587 --> 00:18:53.882
You have no self-respect,
when you still call him CEO.

354
00:18:54.466 --> 00:18:56.760
So what should be said?
Department head?

355
00:18:57.386 --> 00:18:58.303
Oops!
-What happened?

356
00:18:59.138 --> 00:19:00.514
Oops!
-What happened?

357
00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:02.766
Oops!
-What happened?

358
00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.810
What on earth?
- Head of department?

359
00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:06.687
Oops!
-What happened?

360
00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:07.813
What on earth?

361
00:19:22.035 --> 00:19:23.370
Oops!
-What happened?

362
00:19:23.453 --> 00:19:24.496
What on earth?

363
00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:27.332
I really freaked out.

364
00:19:27.833 --> 00:19:29.334
What was it?
- It exploded.

365
00:19:29.418 --> 00:19:30.586
What exploded?

366
00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.380
The body suddenly exploded.
- Did your stomach burst?

367
00:19:33.463 --> 00:19:34.798
Stomach?
-Oh no.

368
00:19:35.757 --> 00:19:39.928
Did your stomach burst?
-The body bounced like a frog.

369
00:19:40.012 --> 00:19:41.513
Why did he suddenly explode?

370
00:19:41.597 --> 00:19:43.473
Skin is everywhere.
- Did your stomach explode?

371
00:19:43.557 --> 00:19:46.310
What the hell? Night!
-We were warned about explosive animals.

372
00:19:46.393 --> 00:19:49.062
His skin is everywhere. A terrible mess.

373
00:19:49.605 --> 00:19:51.857
Did he burst out laughing?

374
00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.525
It smells.
-Terrible slacker.

375
00:19:53.609 --> 00:19:55.444
Where does that lemu come from?
-What smells?

376
00:19:55.527 --> 00:19:56.612
What is it?

377
00:19:56.695 --> 00:19:59.698
Smells like methane
in my old neighborhood.

378
00:19:59.781 --> 00:20:01.283
That's right, that's the smell of methane.

379
00:20:01.366 --> 00:20:03.660
We shouldn't be breathing this.

380
00:20:03.744 --> 00:20:05.579
This is just…
-What the hell?

381
00:20:05.662 --> 00:20:08.040
Perhaps the body was placed like this,
so we can see the explosion.

382
00:20:08.123 --> 00:20:11.543
Wait a minute. Normally
the gas leak detector should sound the alarm.

383
00:20:11.627 --> 00:20:13.712
WAS THE DETECTOR THUMBED
PART OF THE PLAN?

384
00:20:14.338 --> 00:20:17.257
Maybe it was the Singer.
- Let's examine the lips first.

385
00:20:17.341 --> 00:20:18.425
This is really badass.

386
00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:21.261
The smell is too strong.

387
00:20:21.887 --> 00:20:23.305
The mouth is agape.

388
00:20:23.388 --> 00:20:24.973
Oh no.
- Can you open your mouth?

389
00:20:25.057 --> 00:20:28.227
Don't touch it or it will explode.
- The smell is disgusting.

390
00:20:30.938 --> 00:20:31.980
He has an underbite.

391
00:20:32.064 --> 00:20:33.273
What is that?
- Your lips...

392
00:20:33.357 --> 00:20:35.400
There is something in the mouth.
- Mr. Chef can.

393
00:20:35.484 --> 00:20:38.612
He knows how to handle corpses.
He's not normal.

394
00:20:38.695 --> 00:20:41.198
Sloth is intolerable.
- Something was put here.

395
00:20:41.281 --> 00:20:42.783
Disgusting!
-What on earth?

396
00:20:42.866 --> 00:20:43.992
What is it?
- It loosens.

397
00:20:44.076 --> 00:20:45.494
Something was put here.

398
00:20:45.577 --> 00:20:47.246
Disgusting!
-What on earth?

399
00:20:47.329 --> 00:20:48.455
What is it?
- It loosens.

400
00:20:48.538 --> 00:20:50.540
Is it a ground dummy?
- It's a penguin!

401
00:20:50.624 --> 00:20:53.168
Penguin.
- Similar lips were painted on the bodies.

402
00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:54.294
Why?

403
00:20:54.378 --> 00:20:57.422
That's a Russian wooden doll.
-That's right.

404
00:20:57.506 --> 00:20:59.758
Let's count, how many of these are there. Open it.

405
00:20:59.841 --> 00:21:01.093
One.

406
00:21:01.176 --> 00:21:02.261
Two.

407
00:21:02.886 --> 00:21:04.221
Three.

408
00:21:04.304 --> 00:21:05.514
Four.

409
00:21:06.807 --> 00:21:08.684
Five.
- There are five of them.

410
00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:11.687
Five in total?
-Yes.

411
00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.272
Why are there five?

412
00:21:13.355 --> 00:21:15.399
Why five?
- There are five of us.

413
00:21:16.358 --> 00:21:17.776
True. There are five suspects.

414
00:21:18.694 --> 00:21:21.405
Judging by the lips…
-Look at the lips.

415
00:21:21.488 --> 00:21:23.949
He is one of the dolls too.
-Can they somehow...

416
00:21:24.032 --> 00:21:25.033
Exactly.

417
00:21:25.117 --> 00:21:28.078
He was turned into a penguin,
so he is one of the dolls.

418
00:21:28.161 --> 00:21:29.705
So there are six of them.
-Right.

419
00:21:29.788 --> 00:21:33.542
There are six people besides me
including the victim.

420
00:21:33.625 --> 00:21:36.920
There are also six penguins.
-Why are there six of them?

421
00:21:37.004 --> 00:21:39.089
Why is the victim also one of the penguins?

422
00:21:39.172 --> 00:21:44.469
You must be crazy to paint your lips like that
and shoves the doll down its throat.

423
00:21:44.553 --> 00:21:47.431
The killer planned quite a show.

424
00:21:47.514 --> 00:21:53.145
How did the killer make the stomach explode
right moment?

425
00:21:53.228 --> 00:21:55.022
It's… A moment.

426
00:21:55.689 --> 00:21:58.525
It was a planned thing.
- It seems so.

427
00:21:58.608 --> 00:22:00.944
It's hot in here because of the lights.

428
00:22:01.028 --> 00:22:03.864
The stomach was made to explode with a spotlight.

429
00:22:03.947 --> 00:22:05.574
THE SPOTLIGHT POINTED TO THE BODY'S BELLY

430
00:22:05.657 --> 00:22:08.118
Do you remember what the cleaning instructions said?

431
00:22:08.201 --> 00:22:11.788
Carcasses can explode when rotting.
-Old carcasses.

432
00:22:11.872 --> 00:22:15.334
The killer planned everything based on that.

433
00:22:15.417 --> 00:22:18.378
A corpse was pointed to with a light,
to raise the body temperature.

434
00:22:18.462 --> 00:22:20.213
It accelerated the rot.

435
00:22:20.297 --> 00:22:23.925
Otherwise, it would not accumulate in a fresh body
methane quickly enough.

436
00:22:24.009 --> 00:22:26.803
That's why the killer needed 24 hours.

437
00:22:26.887 --> 00:22:28.847
The body had to rot.

438
00:22:29.639 --> 00:22:33.602
The killer's plan
was detailed.

439
00:22:33.685 --> 00:22:38.899
It was the casino's one-year anniversary
the perfect reason to bring everyone to the casino.

440
00:22:38.982 --> 00:22:41.693
Because the killer knew
that the vault shall be opened on that day,

441
00:22:41.777 --> 00:22:44.863
he knew where to commit the murder.

442
00:22:45.572 --> 00:22:47.866
The killer placed the body on the stage -

443
00:22:48.492 --> 00:22:53.497
and aimed the spotlight, because he knew
body in an explosively hot environment.

444
00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:59.044
The killer did the math,
for the body to explode -

445
00:22:59.127 --> 00:23:01.713
with everyone close to the stage.

446
00:23:01.797 --> 00:23:06.718
It was clearly a show,
that everyone had to see -

447
00:23:06.802 --> 00:23:08.929
and where there was a big explosion.

448
00:23:09.513 --> 00:23:13.016
However, I wondered why the killer
prepared this show?

449
00:23:14.893 --> 00:23:18.605
We are looking for more traces left by the killer.

450
00:23:18.688 --> 00:23:20.649
Let's disperse to look for clues.

451
00:23:21.775 --> 00:23:24.236
I will kill whoever did this.

452
00:23:25.779 --> 00:23:27.989
THE OLDEST WOMAN OF THE GROUP HATES THE SMELL

453
00:23:29.407 --> 00:23:31.409
MAYOR JEON'S OFFICE WILL BE INVESTIGATED

454
00:23:34.913 --> 00:23:35.914
Did you find something?

455
00:23:37.457 --> 00:23:38.875
The prediction annoys me.

456
00:23:40.752 --> 00:23:43.839
He had to prepare
to blow up the tomb at any time.

457
00:23:45.382 --> 00:23:49.886
Do you remember the flower he grew?
- It was mentioned in emails in 2021.

458
00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:52.055
We are investigating the emails that have been sent.

459
00:23:52.139 --> 00:23:54.558
Let's see.
-"Mayor Jeon."

460
00:23:54.641 --> 00:23:56.268
EMAIL DISCUSSIONS

461
00:23:56.351 --> 00:23:57.519
What is this?

462
00:23:57.602 --> 00:23:59.688
JUST THINK ABOUT HOW THE CASINO IS EXPLODED

463
00:24:01.148 --> 00:24:04.234
"Collect methane, leak, boom and be done.
Would this work?"

464
00:24:04.317 --> 00:24:07.737
So the mayor knew the risks of methane.
-You knew that.

465
00:24:07.821 --> 00:24:10.699
He wanted to blow it up.
-He wanted a way to destroy it.

466
00:24:10.782 --> 00:24:13.952
When it was done,
he would build a big flower and a stadium -

467
00:24:14.035 --> 00:24:16.121
to become "king",
i.e. for president.

468
00:24:16.705 --> 00:24:19.791
Madam Mayor,
do you want to be president?

469
00:24:19.875 --> 00:24:24.421
Of course. I've always dreamed of it.
-When were you going to blow up the casino?

470
00:24:24.504 --> 00:24:26.673
You've got blasting wrong.

471
00:24:26.756 --> 00:24:31.094
I'm looking for a way just because
if the prediction should be followed.

472
00:24:31.178 --> 00:24:33.430
Let's say you needed methane.

473
00:24:33.513 --> 00:24:37.726
You would need a place to store it,
to be ready to blow up the casino.

474
00:24:37.809 --> 00:24:40.312
It didn't go that way. This I know.

475
00:24:40.395 --> 00:24:45.233
You have to install on such a dump
a device that collects methane,

476
00:24:45.317 --> 00:24:49.029
so that the place can be used for something else.
The device must be installed…

477
00:24:49.112 --> 00:24:50.947
To collect methane?
-So.

478
00:24:51.031 --> 00:24:55.535
The device must be installed,
so that the construction work can be approved.

479
00:24:55.619 --> 00:24:56.620
I don't know anything else.

480
00:24:56.703 --> 00:25:00.790
Is there a methane capture device installed here?
-Is this where it was installed?

481
00:25:00.874 --> 00:25:03.293
Probably.
The casino was built on a landfill.

482
00:25:03.376 --> 00:25:05.420
The device is somewhere, but you don't know where.

483
00:25:06.087 --> 00:25:09.341
Exploding the device
would destroy the whole casino.

484
00:25:10.217 --> 00:25:12.677
In general, you have to wait 30 years,

485
00:25:12.761 --> 00:25:15.764
before going to landfill
can build anything.

486
00:25:15.847 --> 00:25:18.892
The casino was built before that.

487
00:25:18.975 --> 00:25:23.063
Think how much methane
under the casino is formed.

488
00:25:23.146 --> 00:25:28.485
I assumed there must be a device in the area,
which collects it.

489
00:25:29.778 --> 00:25:34.032
All in this case
leads back to the landfill.

490
00:25:34.115 --> 00:25:39.746
It is clear that it has been done here
very secret business.

491
00:25:40.705 --> 00:25:41.957
Now.

492
00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:47.629
Which of the leads you've collected
do you think is important to mention?

493
00:25:47.712 --> 00:25:51.758
Anything worth doing
investigate further or which refers to…

494
00:25:51.841 --> 00:25:54.094
What the hell?
- I still smell the gas.

495
00:25:54.177 --> 00:25:56.596
Where does the smell come from?
- Methane is still leaking.

496
00:25:57.180 --> 00:25:59.391
We're all going to die this way.

497
00:25:59.474 --> 00:26:01.059
I can't stand this.
-What the hell?

498
00:26:01.142 --> 00:26:03.186
What if we suffocate to death?

499
00:26:03.270 --> 00:26:06.064
It can't be true.
-Should we get out of here?

500
00:26:06.773 --> 00:26:08.191
Still leaking gas.

501
00:26:11.486 --> 00:26:15.198
What if we all start coughing
as bad as Singer?

502
00:26:15.282 --> 00:26:17.117
I might pass out.

503
00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:22.789
Methane is leaking from somewhere.

504
00:26:23.790 --> 00:26:25.375
Shall we go look over there?

505
00:26:25.458 --> 00:26:26.960
IS THERE A METHANE LEAK SOMEWHERE?

506
00:26:27.460 --> 00:26:30.755
Does it come from here?
- Go see what's there.

507
00:26:31.798 --> 00:26:36.052
Let's investigate quickly, or we die.

508
00:26:36.136 --> 00:26:38.805
Find the source of the leak.
-It's not here.

509
00:26:38.888 --> 00:26:40.932
Not here.
-Is this the end of us?

510
00:26:41.016 --> 00:26:43.059
The smell is coming from somewhere.

511
00:26:43.727 --> 00:26:45.270
Pull the curtains all the way open.

512
00:26:46.938 --> 00:26:48.440
Did you find something?
-I found it.

513
00:26:48.523 --> 00:26:49.899
Really?
- Let's open this.

514
00:26:52.277 --> 00:26:53.570
Really?
- Let's open this.

515
00:26:54.195 --> 00:26:55.322
WILL IT OPEN?

516
00:26:55.405 --> 00:26:56.489
And not.

517
00:27:00.952 --> 00:27:02.746
GAS CONTROL ROOM

518
00:27:03.747 --> 00:27:06.207
OTHER VALVES ARE CLOSED

519
00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.792
It can't be true.

520
00:27:07.876 --> 00:27:10.170
The valve is left open!
- There was a leak here.

521
00:27:10.253 --> 00:27:11.629
Look.
-What is that?

522
00:27:11.713 --> 00:27:13.882
Close the valve!
- It's leaking methane!

523
00:27:14.466 --> 00:27:17.510
This is a gas collection device.
- It was a methane leak.

524
00:27:17.594 --> 00:27:18.803
Beyond belief.
-Head hurts.

525
00:27:18.887 --> 00:27:22.098
The killer released methane,
so that it would cause confusion.

526
00:27:22.182 --> 00:27:25.352
Right. So the killer knew about this room.
-True.

527
00:27:25.935 --> 00:27:28.480
The killer knew.
-Hello, Singer.

528
00:27:29.564 --> 00:27:31.191
I knew you doubted me.

529
00:27:31.274 --> 00:27:35.528
You performed on that stage.
-True, but I've never been here.

530
00:27:35.612 --> 00:27:37.072
I'm not a staff member.

531
00:27:37.155 --> 00:27:39.282
There are other gases such as oxygen.

532
00:27:39.366 --> 00:27:41.368
Could we not release phytoncides?

533
00:27:41.451 --> 00:27:44.037
The killer installed a timer
to release methane.

534
00:27:44.120 --> 00:27:46.623
The methane valve was open.
- Planned thing.

535
00:27:46.706 --> 00:27:51.753
The killer planned it so that the show
would start exactly 24 hours after the murder.

536
00:27:52.712 --> 00:27:54.798
This…
- Very thorough.

537
00:27:54.881 --> 00:27:56.341
Or so…
-Too meticulous.

538
00:27:56.424 --> 00:27:59.427
The author must be calculating.

539
00:27:59.511 --> 00:28:02.514
There is something we don't notice.

540
00:28:02.597 --> 00:28:05.183
It wasn't just about his death.

541
00:28:05.266 --> 00:28:08.395
You all had to die.
-He wanted to kill everyone.

542
00:28:08.478 --> 00:28:11.106
There are no windows here,
and gas a year out.

543
00:28:11.189 --> 00:28:12.857
You had to die too.

544
00:28:14.651 --> 00:28:16.694
Who would want to kill you all?

545
00:28:16.778 --> 00:28:18.571
Did the killer plan suicide?

546
00:28:18.655 --> 00:28:20.573
Maybe it was a murder-suicide.
-Or maybe...

547
00:28:20.657 --> 00:28:22.492
Someone dreams of a new world.

548
00:28:22.575 --> 00:28:24.119
Who was that?
-Chef.

549
00:28:25.286 --> 00:28:26.538
We needed a new world.

550
00:28:26.621 --> 00:28:29.416
Did we have to be human sacrifices?
-Not again.

551
00:28:29.499 --> 00:28:31.209
Messianic Church.
- Me too?

552
00:28:31.292 --> 00:28:33.461
Five people had gathered at the casino.

553
00:28:33.545 --> 00:28:36.714
Including the body, there are six penguins.

554
00:28:36.798 --> 00:28:39.300
What does that number mean?

555
00:28:39.384 --> 00:28:45.473
The total number was six
including the body and the killer.

556
00:28:45.557 --> 00:28:48.226
"I have arranged death,

557
00:28:48.309 --> 00:28:52.814
chose the people who will come with me,
and we will leave this world together."

558
00:28:53.690 --> 00:28:58.319
All cards are now on the table.

559
00:28:58.403 --> 00:29:02.157
The killer must be caught
like playing a card game.

560
00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:05.243
I believe some of the leads
is still to be presented.

561
00:29:05.326 --> 00:29:08.288
That's why I would
give everyone a body check.

562
00:29:08.371 --> 00:29:10.832
Madam Mayor, stand up.
-Clear.

563
00:29:10.915 --> 00:29:12.375
ALL SUSPECTS WILL BE INVESTIGATED

564
00:29:13.293 --> 00:29:14.961
There's nothing up your sleeves.

565
00:29:16.379 --> 00:29:18.965
The pockets are empty too.

566
00:29:19.758 --> 00:29:21.092
Your turn.
-Wait.

567
00:29:21.176 --> 00:29:23.094
What now?
-I'll show you what I've got.

568
00:29:23.178 --> 00:29:24.721
What do you mean?
-I'm shy.

569
00:29:24.804 --> 00:29:25.930
Don't now.
-Wait a minute.

570
00:29:26.014 --> 00:29:27.348
The jewelry is not ordinary.

571
00:29:30.351 --> 00:29:31.811
A NECKLACE CLOSE TO THE HEART

572
00:29:31.895 --> 00:29:33.563
What now?

573
00:29:34.147 --> 00:29:37.984
This symbolizes my conviction.
I was hoping I didn't have to show this.

574
00:29:39.694 --> 00:29:43.156
Are you sure that's all?
-What did the Jeweler have?

575
00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:45.241
What is it?

576
00:29:45.742 --> 00:29:48.870
"Rehti, I'm sorry."
-Is he sorry?

577
00:29:48.953 --> 00:29:51.706
"I ask for your forgiveness when we meet."

578
00:29:51.790 --> 00:29:54.626
THE JEWELERY IS ENGRAVED
SISK'S FACE AND MESSAGE

579
00:29:54.709 --> 00:29:56.461
"I ask for your forgiveness when we meet."

580
00:29:56.544 --> 00:29:58.546
Were you going to kill yourself?
- The sister is dead!

581
00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:03.426
A reunion and an apology.
- But he's dead!

582
00:30:04.719 --> 00:30:05.637
So what?

583
00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:08.306
Maybe he wants to get to his sister.

584
00:30:08.389 --> 00:30:11.309
The killer planned the murder and suicide.
-And failed.

585
00:30:11.392 --> 00:30:14.145
He didn't die.
-Right.

586
00:30:14.229 --> 00:30:15.897
True.
- It can't be.

587
00:30:15.980 --> 00:30:19.317
He's clearly still grieving.
-"I ask for forgiveness when we meet."

588
00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:22.445
When did he hope to meet again
and what did you want to apologize for?

589
00:30:22.529 --> 00:30:24.155
I'll tell you about the necklace.

590
00:30:24.239 --> 00:30:29.160
As you know, I have tried to live
live life like my sister taught me.

591
00:30:29.244 --> 00:30:32.455
But since it was his life,

592
00:30:32.539 --> 00:30:37.001
I had to cheat
and sell imitations to make money.

593
00:30:37.085 --> 00:30:42.382
I still made tea in memory of his teachings
this piece of jewelry I'm wearing.

594
00:30:42.966 --> 00:30:46.344
It came to light by chance now,
when we consider

595
00:30:46.427 --> 00:30:49.722
did the killer want
also takes his own life.

596
00:30:49.806 --> 00:30:51.891
I didn't understand anything about that.

597
00:30:53.059 --> 00:30:54.310
Listen more closely.

598
00:30:55.144 --> 00:30:57.313
Don't be mean to him!

599
00:30:58.439 --> 00:30:59.440
What now?

600
00:30:59.524 --> 00:31:01.234
Oh you.
-What is it?

601
00:31:01.317 --> 00:31:02.735
What now?
-Well?

602
00:31:03.695 --> 00:31:06.823
I found this in the singer's back pocket.
-Which one?

603
00:31:07.574 --> 00:31:09.576
EARLIER DURING THE CARDIGAN INSPECTION

604
00:31:11.703 --> 00:31:13.413
DID HE FIND SOMETHING?

605
00:31:15.081 --> 00:31:17.041
MEDICAL OPINION

606
00:31:20.003 --> 00:31:21.379
NAME: SINGER KIM

607
00:31:21.462 --> 00:31:25.633
He has incurable lung cancer!

608
00:31:26.301 --> 00:31:27.385
The singer…

609
00:31:31.014 --> 00:31:32.390
Are you serious?

610
00:31:32.473 --> 00:31:35.435
KIM SINGER COUGHED VIOLENTLY ALL DAY,

611
00:31:38.479 --> 00:31:40.940
BECAUSE SHE HAS INCURABLE LUNG CANCER

612
00:31:42.525 --> 00:31:43.735
Look at this blood.

613
00:31:44.319 --> 00:31:45.737
HE EVEN COUGHED BLOOD!

614
00:31:45.820 --> 00:31:49.032
Does it stick?
-You can't be that heartless.

615
00:31:49.115 --> 00:31:50.700
Madam Mayor.
- Let's bury him.

616
00:31:50.783 --> 00:31:52.577
Lung cancer is not contagious.

617
00:31:54.454 --> 00:31:57.332
“Even though family members have died
to the same disease,

618
00:31:57.415 --> 00:31:58.958
it must not be hereditary.

619
00:31:59.042 --> 00:32:01.461
The culprit is apparently
exposure to chemicals."

620
00:32:01.544 --> 00:32:04.797
“Incurable, cannot be cut.
Life expectancy is eight months."

621
00:32:04.881 --> 00:32:08.801
His family died of lung cancer,
and he too will die soon.

622
00:32:08.885 --> 00:32:12.138
It can motivate murder and suicide.
-Indeed.

623
00:32:12.221 --> 00:32:13.556
Others must die too.

624
00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:15.725
No.
I want to live even one more day.

625
00:32:15.808 --> 00:32:17.936
Clear.
- I can still debut in the USA.

626
00:32:18.019 --> 00:32:20.688
You might be lying.
-He wants to live -

627
00:32:20.772 --> 00:32:24.567
even one more day to implement
his dream of performing in the USA.

628
00:32:24.651 --> 00:32:26.736
That dream was shattered.
-True.

629
00:32:26.819 --> 00:32:29.530
What about Mr. Merikrot?

630
00:32:29.614 --> 00:32:34.702
He was a fisherman,
so he must have eaten contaminated fish.

631
00:32:34.786 --> 00:32:40.375
That would explain asthma, which is known to be
aftereffect of heavy metal poisoning.

632
00:32:40.458 --> 00:32:44.420
Death would not grieve him,
because that way he would get to his wife.

633
00:32:44.504 --> 00:32:45.964
And…
- How could that not be sad?

634
00:32:46.881 --> 00:32:48.633
Would it hurt if you died?
-Of course.

635
00:32:48.716 --> 00:32:51.928
Even if you could get to your wife.
- My wife would like me to live.

636
00:32:52.011 --> 00:32:53.596
Really?
-Of course.

637
00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:54.722
Clear.

638
00:32:54.806 --> 00:32:58.476
Let's consider the possibility
that Chef Jang is to blame.

639
00:32:58.559 --> 00:33:01.854
We await that day.
Is it possible that his faith -

640
00:33:01.938 --> 00:33:03.564
forced him to murder?

641
00:33:03.648 --> 00:33:07.443
I think so. That's what cults are.
- He belongs to a cult.

642
00:33:07.527 --> 00:33:11.197
Why would a killer want to
kill us all at once?

643
00:33:11.698 --> 00:33:13.700
Why the five of us?

644
00:33:14.450 --> 00:33:18.162
He targeted a certain group of people.
Let's find out why we were chosen.

645
00:33:18.246 --> 00:33:20.289
It had to be one of the five of you.

646
00:33:20.373 --> 00:33:24.544
That's why the killer wasn't allowed here
other guests, only you.

647
00:33:25.044 --> 00:33:29.674
It all started in a landfill.

648
00:33:30.675 --> 00:33:35.221
In 2000, my father built a landfill
to get funding from the state -

649
00:33:35.304 --> 00:33:39.058
and to cover up
the city's funding deficit.

650
00:33:39.142 --> 00:33:41.185
The singer was desperate for money -

651
00:33:41.269 --> 00:33:44.272
and participated
for illegal waste disposal.

652
00:33:44.355 --> 00:33:47.734
And don't forget,
that Mr. Merikrotti was also involved.

653
00:33:47.817 --> 00:33:50.403
You are not innocent victims.
Each of you had a role to play.

654
00:33:50.486 --> 00:33:54.282
Do you remember what Mr. Kingfisher did?
- I sold contaminated fish.

655
00:33:54.365 --> 00:33:57.452
That's why many people
ate contaminated fish in restaurants -

656
00:33:57.535 --> 00:34:01.456
and were exposed to heavy metals.
You were all part of a chain reaction.

657
00:34:02.373 --> 00:34:05.334
When the World Ball tournament was held
in 2002,

658
00:34:05.418 --> 00:34:09.047
rumors of an epidemic would have driven it away
anything, and it would have been a disaster.

659
00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:13.634
Chef Jang made a mistake
diagnoses and prevented the truth from spreading.

660
00:34:13.718 --> 00:34:18.097
Who hid the environmental report,

661
00:34:18.181 --> 00:34:21.726
encouraged forced relocation
and took a share of the money?

662
00:34:22.310 --> 00:34:25.188
Jeweler An.
He was a government official then.

663
00:34:25.271 --> 00:34:28.149
Your sister may have been a victim,
but you are the opposite.

664
00:34:28.232 --> 00:34:31.069
For four seasons, Jeon collected his offering -

665
00:34:31.152 --> 00:34:34.447
ordering to bury those,
who did not give their consent.

666
00:34:34.530 --> 00:34:37.658
Like his father, Mayor Jeon
believed the predictions blindly -

667
00:34:37.742 --> 00:34:39.452
and planted a flower in the landfill.

668
00:34:39.535 --> 00:34:41.579
That's why the casino is shaped like a flower.

669
00:34:41.662 --> 00:34:45.500
What really unites these people?

670
00:34:46.167 --> 00:34:50.671
Intentionally or not,
they were complicit in the tragedy.

671
00:34:50.755 --> 00:34:53.299
They all had blood on their hands.

672
00:34:54.509 --> 00:34:57.095
Who started the whole thing?

673
00:34:57.178 --> 00:35:01.766
Mayor Jeon's father,
former mayor Four term Jeon.

674
00:35:01.849 --> 00:35:06.395
Since the dead cannot be held responsible,
the killer targeted the daughter.

675
00:35:06.479 --> 00:35:08.689
The jeweler talks openly about his feelings.

676
00:35:08.773 --> 00:35:10.525
In his diary?
-So.

677
00:35:10.608 --> 00:35:13.778
"Second of July 2019.
Four season Jeon is dead.

678
00:35:13.861 --> 00:35:16.572
There will be a daughter
The next mayor of Heoyoung City.

679
00:35:16.656 --> 00:35:19.742
Why is the world like this?
Well, there's no such thing as justice."

680
00:35:19.826 --> 00:35:24.580
"Mayor Jeon became mayor.
I donate money to him every year."

681
00:35:24.664 --> 00:35:28.709
“I hope through our enemy's daughter
i can solve your death -

682
00:35:28.793 --> 00:35:34.132
and those dark deeds,
which he continues for his father."

683
00:35:35.216 --> 00:35:40.096
He deposited 70 billion won
to get closer to the CEO.

684
00:35:40.179 --> 00:35:42.014
He made donations to the mayor -

685
00:35:42.098 --> 00:35:45.601
to unravel the secrets.
-He's messing with my things.

686
00:35:45.685 --> 00:35:49.814
He wouldn't have minded
explodes with its 70 billion won.

687
00:35:49.897 --> 00:35:53.943
If you don't mind losing that amount,
he would not want to live anymore.

688
00:35:54.026 --> 00:35:55.945
Why wouldn't I want to live?

689
00:35:56.487 --> 00:35:57.947
I want to live.

690
00:35:58.030 --> 00:36:04.245
So that the killer who committed this murder
knowing you all are criminals,

691
00:36:04.328 --> 00:36:07.331
he knows your story inside and out.
-He knows our history.

692
00:36:07.415 --> 00:36:09.041
Certainly.
-There must be some connection.

693
00:36:09.125 --> 00:36:12.753
How did the killer get all your information?

694
00:36:13.337 --> 00:36:18.509
So that the killer knows that each suspect
was somehow responsible for the deaths,

695
00:36:18.593 --> 00:36:24.557
he certainly was
familiarized with the environmental report.

696
00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:27.268
The report contained a summary
for each case.

697
00:36:27.351 --> 00:36:31.772
Maybe it all started
from heavy metal poisoning -

698
00:36:31.856 --> 00:36:34.233
and proceeded to eat the tainted meat.

699
00:36:34.317 --> 00:36:37.320
Then everything was covered up
with wrong diagnoses.

700
00:36:37.403 --> 00:36:39.739
Each of us relates to these cases.

701
00:36:39.822 --> 00:36:42.992
Someone who knew about the report
and our involvement,

702
00:36:43.075 --> 00:36:45.244
has gathered us together today.

703
00:36:46.329 --> 00:36:48.664
If we think about the crime scene,

704
00:36:48.748 --> 00:36:53.753
the killer delivered his message by blowing up
CEO Kim's stomach.

705
00:36:53.836 --> 00:36:57.215
The killer practically declared,
that they were all responsible.

706
00:36:57.298 --> 00:37:03.638
Anyone responsible for the tragedy,
would be punished by murder and suicide.

707
00:37:03.721 --> 00:37:05.556
Otherwise we'll die.
- That was the plan.

708
00:37:06.641 --> 00:37:09.227
The author knew about the documents.
-He got them.

709
00:37:10.478 --> 00:37:12.897
The mayor was entitled to the documents.

710
00:37:12.980 --> 00:37:15.441
They were found in the archive
next to his study.

711
00:37:15.524 --> 00:37:18.194
He would have easily gotten hold of them.
-True.

712
00:37:18.277 --> 00:37:20.363
These are from the archives.
-Really?

713
00:37:20.446 --> 00:37:23.241
The cabinet read the 21st century.
-That's because of the effort.

714
00:37:23.324 --> 00:37:24.450
In addition…

715
00:37:24.533 --> 00:37:27.453
Jeweler An.
- He knew about the transfer plan.

716
00:37:27.536 --> 00:37:31.457
He could have copied these
before resigning.

717
00:37:31.540 --> 00:37:36.295
A jeweler had a copy
from the environmental report.

718
00:37:36.379 --> 00:37:40.174
He had this information
and a strong motive to kill.

719
00:37:41.926 --> 00:37:46.639
Sorry to blame you,
but the evidence points to you.

720
00:37:46.722 --> 00:37:48.140
Gotta ask.

721
00:37:48.224 --> 00:37:52.228
Why have I become the prime suspect?
With what logic?

722
00:37:52.311 --> 00:37:55.815
Simply put
we are all responsible for what happened.

723
00:37:55.898 --> 00:37:57.817
Yes, you too.

724
00:37:57.900 --> 00:38:00.945
Because your sister died because of what happened,

725
00:38:01.028 --> 00:38:04.323
you get the most guilt.
-What did I do that hurt people?

726
00:38:04.907 --> 00:38:07.410
Transfer plan.
-What about it?

727
00:38:07.493 --> 00:38:11.080
I was only guilty of embezzlement.
-You were a civil servant at the time.

728
00:38:11.580 --> 00:38:13.708
Agreement…
-Bong-cheon collected the signatures.

729
00:38:13.791 --> 00:38:16.377
Collecting was harmful.
- It wasn't me.

730
00:38:16.460 --> 00:38:20.006
I just embezzled money.
- Or so.

731
00:38:20.089 --> 00:38:23.968
I don't even know why I'm being accused.
-Why do you want to apologize to your sister?

732
00:38:24.051 --> 00:38:27.805
Because I didn't live a straight life.
Not really because of my act.

733
00:38:27.888 --> 00:38:29.682
We assume that your wrongdoing -

734
00:38:29.765 --> 00:38:35.021
related to the transfer plan.
-Why does that make me guilty?

735
00:38:36.981 --> 00:38:40.151
Please provide evidence, not theories.
-Evidence?

736
00:38:40.234 --> 00:38:45.281
Solid evidence, not mere assumptions.
- The people here are proof.

737
00:38:45.364 --> 00:38:46.991
How so?
- These documents -

738
00:38:47.074 --> 00:38:50.619
and you participated in the transfer plan.

739
00:38:50.703 --> 00:38:53.247
No one reads
such forms meticulously.

740
00:38:53.331 --> 00:38:56.500
You still got them.
-So.

741
00:38:56.584 --> 00:38:58.377
The same applies to Mayor Jeon.

742
00:38:58.461 --> 00:39:02.214
That's why we accused you both,
but only one got angry -

743
00:39:02.298 --> 00:39:04.467
and the other is unwell.

744
00:39:04.550 --> 00:39:07.178
I think that's your breakup.

745
00:39:08.512 --> 00:39:12.183
The jeweler certainly knew
deep regret and guilt for

746
00:39:12.266 --> 00:39:15.311
that betrayed his sister's environmental ideal -

747
00:39:15.394 --> 00:39:17.605
because of their poor decisions.

748
00:39:17.688 --> 00:39:22.360
His plan was to get out
to his sister and beg for forgiveness,

749
00:39:22.443 --> 00:39:28.657
and because of that he drifted
to kill everyone and himself.

750
00:39:28.741 --> 00:39:32.703
Assume for the sake of fairness,
that the Mayor is a killer.

751
00:39:32.787 --> 00:39:36.457
He had a tape,
with which he entered the vault.

752
00:39:36.540 --> 00:39:37.708
This is Bong-cheon Kim.

753
00:39:37.792 --> 00:39:40.044
THE MAYOR HAD A VOICE,
WHO OPENED THE VAULT

754
00:39:40.127 --> 00:39:42.797
He also knew
that methane was flammable,

755
00:39:42.880 --> 00:39:45.007
because he was told that in the email.

756
00:39:45.091 --> 00:39:48.260
I just wanted this.
That was my only goal.

757
00:39:48.344 --> 00:39:51.931
I wanted to destroy this.
- Quick question.

758
00:39:52.014 --> 00:39:55.976
He blackmailed you with this.
Why did you go back to your study with it?

759
00:39:56.060 --> 00:39:58.562
On the evening of the 7th… So I stole.
- You stole it.

760
00:39:58.646 --> 00:40:02.817
I knew
that he processed payments at 11 p.m.

761
00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:05.361
I thought
to sneak in and take this.

762
00:40:05.444 --> 00:40:07.738
It was around 23:50.

763
00:40:07.822 --> 00:40:10.616
Did you say 23:50?
-Yeah.

764
00:40:10.699 --> 00:40:12.243
Then...
- Pretty late.

765
00:40:12.326 --> 00:40:14.412
It's almost death time.

766
00:40:14.495 --> 00:40:17.081
The CEO's room was empty at the time.

767
00:40:17.164 --> 00:40:19.542
I snuck in
assuming he handles payments.

768
00:40:19.625 --> 00:40:22.336
I left with this notebook.
- Oh, at 11:50 p.m.?

769
00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:25.214
I left at midnight.
- He might not have seen the killer.

770
00:40:25.297 --> 00:40:27.967
After all, the vault is soundproof.
- The killer could have been there.

771
00:40:28.050 --> 00:40:32.721
Let's think about the gas leak.
He planned to blow up the casino.

772
00:40:32.805 --> 00:40:37.643
Maybe he finally did
the prophecy he received from his shaman.

773
00:40:37.726 --> 00:40:41.897
he knew
that the vault would protect him from the explosion.

774
00:40:41.981 --> 00:40:45.359
Our reasoning is going in that direction.

775
00:40:45.443 --> 00:40:47.736
After killing everyone,
which were related to the landfill,

776
00:40:47.820 --> 00:40:50.614
he would be left behind.
-Right.

777
00:40:50.698 --> 00:40:54.869
We all had a motive
kill Bong-cheon Kim -

778
00:40:54.952 --> 00:40:59.081
and also a reason to take our own lives,
except for the Mayor.

779
00:40:59.165 --> 00:41:01.834
I don't want to die.
- I don't think it was him.

780
00:41:01.917 --> 00:41:03.210
It can't be him.

781
00:41:03.294 --> 00:41:07.339
Based on that
Mayor Jeon cannot be a suspect.

782
00:41:07.423 --> 00:41:09.175
One more thing.

783
00:41:09.258 --> 00:41:12.052
We can't yet
to exclude Merikrott from bills.

784
00:41:12.136 --> 00:41:13.596
Do you remember Constable Hyeon?

785
00:41:13.679 --> 00:41:15.723
He explored the dump.
-Right.

786
00:41:15.806 --> 00:41:18.684
It is possible that Constable Hyeon -

787
00:41:18.767 --> 00:41:21.687
reported his discovery to Jang the sea urchin
before his death.

788
00:41:21.770 --> 00:41:25.441
He might have had a crush on him
the same information as the other two.

789
00:41:25.524 --> 00:41:28.652
What exactly happened to your wife?

790
00:41:28.736 --> 00:41:31.238
Did he die because of the abuse?

791
00:41:31.322 --> 00:41:35.826
That's what I thought at first.
He had been badly beaten.

792
00:41:35.910 --> 00:41:40.581
His doctor's report was
among his other belongings.

793
00:41:40.664 --> 00:41:46.086
I met Chef Jang,
when he started working here.

794
00:41:46.170 --> 00:41:51.926
His name was rare,
and then I remembered everything.

795
00:41:52.009 --> 00:41:55.721
Did you dig up the doctor's report?
-No, I just saw it again.

796
00:41:55.804 --> 00:41:57.765
His name sounded familiar.

797
00:41:57.848 --> 00:42:01.143
I realized that
when I read my wife's medical report.

798
00:42:01.227 --> 00:42:03.229
That's when I understood.

799
00:42:03.312 --> 00:42:07.149
Before his death
my wife went to the doctor because of pain.

800
00:42:07.233 --> 00:42:10.152
We didn't think so,
because the diagnosis was flu.

801
00:42:10.236 --> 00:42:15.199
That is, before you saw Chef Jang
a medical report issued by

802
00:42:15.282 --> 00:42:19.954
you believed to have been the cause of your wife's death
abuse, not heavy metal poisoning.

803
00:42:20.037 --> 00:42:22.873
I didn't know about it when he died.
It didn't occur to me.

804
00:42:22.957 --> 00:42:25.876
I avoided death
after the abuse of the nip button.

805
00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:28.128
We already confirmed earlier,

806
00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:33.217
that Merikrot's wife died after eating
the fish he catches and sells.

807
00:42:33.300 --> 00:42:38.305
In our reasoning, it is important for us to consider,

808
00:42:38.389 --> 00:42:43.185
who wanted to die
after killing everyone else here.

809
00:42:43.269 --> 00:42:48.983
Let's think about crimes,
which resulted in tragic deaths.

810
00:42:49.066 --> 00:42:51.360
Who participated knowingly, like me?

811
00:42:52.027 --> 00:42:54.405
THESE THREE COMMITTED THE CRIMES KNOWINGLY

812
00:42:54.488 --> 00:42:57.491
Of course, I feel bad because of Merikrot.
-His act was unintentional.

813
00:42:57.575 --> 00:43:00.911
He didn't know.
- Didn't know he sold contaminated fish.

814
00:43:01.662 --> 00:43:04.748
I think he feels guilty
more than others.

815
00:43:04.832 --> 00:43:07.918
Imagine how he felt,
when he realized -

816
00:43:08.002 --> 00:43:10.379
of having caused his wife's death.

817
00:43:10.462 --> 00:43:13.549
Then you want to die.
- The guilt was unbearable.

818
00:43:13.632 --> 00:43:14.883
Listen.

819
00:43:14.967 --> 00:43:20.222
I learned about heavy metal poisoning
only after the death of the boss.

820
00:43:20.306 --> 00:43:26.145
Only today I heard the truth
about the events of my old neighborhood.

821
00:43:26.228 --> 00:43:30.357
The medical report shows that the wife
there were a lot of heavy metals in the blood.

822
00:43:30.441 --> 00:43:33.444
Because of that, he could have
dig deeper.

823
00:43:33.527 --> 00:43:35.362
I think he might have known.

824
00:43:35.446 --> 00:43:38.365
He claims
that he didn't know about heavy metal poisoning.

825
00:43:38.449 --> 00:43:41.285
A killer could tell a similar lie.

826
00:43:42.077 --> 00:43:44.038
I wanted to ask something.

827
00:43:44.121 --> 00:43:45.914
Back to your asthma medication.

828
00:43:45.998 --> 00:43:47.625
Why did you throw away the medicine?

829
00:43:48.250 --> 00:43:50.336
You won't die without medicine?

830
00:43:50.961 --> 00:43:54.048
He doesn't need asthma medicine anymore.

831
00:43:54.131 --> 00:43:57.968
I didn't throw them away.
-Then why were they in the trash?

832
00:43:58.052 --> 00:44:01.263
Two of the bottles were empty, one was not.
- There was still medicine in one.

833
00:44:01.347 --> 00:44:04.058
I understand that it was not empty,
but I didn't know.

834
00:44:04.141 --> 00:44:07.353
How much was left?
- It was half full.

835
00:44:07.436 --> 00:44:09.980
Why did you throw it away?
- Because it's pointless.

836
00:44:10.064 --> 00:44:13.067
He no longer needs asthma medication.

837
00:44:13.150 --> 00:44:16.654
I doubt as much
Mr. Merikrottia and Mrs. Korukauppia.

838
00:44:16.737 --> 00:44:19.865
I believe there are still leads.
Let's keep digging.

839
00:44:19.948 --> 00:44:23.327
Now. Let's continue.
-Clear.

840
00:44:23.410 --> 00:44:25.954
Why did he throw away his medicine?

841
00:44:28.082 --> 00:44:30.626
WILL THEY FIND CRUCIAL EVIDENCE?

842
00:44:30.709 --> 00:44:31.835
Let's see.

843
00:44:34.254 --> 00:44:35.923
There has to be something more here.

844
00:44:40.052 --> 00:44:41.387
Let's see.

845
00:44:42.054 --> 00:44:43.347
This is for marking.

846
00:44:43.430 --> 00:44:44.682
SEA CORP FLUORESCENT OINTMENT

847
00:44:46.141 --> 00:44:47.142
What is this?

848
00:44:48.310 --> 00:44:50.354
Oh, it's used for this.

849
00:44:51.146 --> 00:44:53.982
How does it work?
-This is how he marks the cards.

850
00:44:57.152 --> 00:44:59.446
Why does he go to so much trouble?
-Listen, Detective.

851
00:45:00.072 --> 00:45:02.324
The killer had
two possible goals.

852
00:45:02.408 --> 00:45:06.036
Either he wanted to show us the murder
or kill us all.

853
00:45:06.120 --> 00:45:09.039
Which is more important?

854
00:45:09.540 --> 00:45:11.750
Presentation of the murder…
- I think so.

855
00:45:11.834 --> 00:45:14.711
The killer wanted everyone here to know,
what they had done.

856
00:45:16.463 --> 00:45:17.881
Did he spread this somewhere?

857
00:45:18.507 --> 00:45:20.884
Maybe he left a mark.
-What do you mean?

858
00:45:23.178 --> 00:45:25.514
Maybe the UV light will reveal something.

859
00:45:26.306 --> 00:45:27.975
Like what?
- A timer, for example.

860
00:45:28.058 --> 00:45:30.060
The cream in the cards
could pass into the hands.

861
00:45:30.644 --> 00:45:34.940
After his death
the gas had to be released with a delay.

862
00:45:35.023 --> 00:45:36.900
The killer wanted us to think about it.

863
00:45:36.984 --> 00:45:39.653
You had to remember the crimes,
what would you die for.

864
00:45:39.736 --> 00:45:42.448
The author actually sent a message.
-Absolutely.

865
00:45:42.531 --> 00:45:44.700
At the cost of his own life?

866
00:45:49.288 --> 00:45:50.539
Can I look at your hands?

867
00:45:53.917 --> 00:45:56.503
HE EXAMINED THE SEA OCT'S JANG'S HANDS

868
00:45:59.047 --> 00:46:00.716
Do you?
- I need glasses.

869
00:46:00.799 --> 00:46:04.720
When a card shark cheats,
he marks the cards with that cream.

870
00:46:05.679 --> 00:46:07.598
Look at the conclusive evidence.

871
00:46:07.681 --> 00:46:09.099
can i

872
00:46:09.183 --> 00:46:10.267
Yeah.
-Like a trigger.

873
00:46:14.062 --> 00:46:16.690
COULD IT BE?

874
00:46:17.608 --> 00:46:19.735
Sorry about this.

875
00:46:24.156 --> 00:46:25.157
Like a trigger.

876
00:46:25.240 --> 00:46:26.700
THE GAS CONTROL ROOM WILL BE INVESTIGATED

877
00:46:26.783 --> 00:46:27.826
We all relate to it.

878
00:46:30.037 --> 00:46:31.163
Gun.

879
00:46:32.080 --> 00:46:33.749
You can only see it with special glasses.

880
00:46:33.832 --> 00:46:35.876
This light also reveals it.

881
00:46:35.959 --> 00:46:37.961
Where is the gun?
- I have cream in my hand.

882
00:46:38.837 --> 00:46:40.506
The light reveals it.

883
00:46:40.589 --> 00:46:43.300
What did you touch?
-I mark the cards with cream.

884
00:46:43.383 --> 00:46:45.385
Ointment.
-That's how I stage the other players.

885
00:46:45.469 --> 00:46:47.930
We were both at the same table yesterday.

886
00:46:48.013 --> 00:46:50.140
Let's say you spread it with your hands.

887
00:46:50.224 --> 00:46:53.268
If you are guilty,
the cream sticks to everything you touch.

888
00:46:53.352 --> 00:46:54.895
Wait and see.
-Maybe he left traces.

889
00:46:55.771 --> 00:46:56.939
You don't know that.

890
00:46:57.022 --> 00:46:58.732
MURDER WEAPON UNDER INVESTIGATION

891
00:47:03.237 --> 00:47:04.655
Should this be done in the dark?

892
00:47:04.738 --> 00:47:05.656
NO TRACE

893
00:47:05.739 --> 00:47:06.865
That's all.

894
00:47:06.949 --> 00:47:09.576
THE VALVE TIMER WILL BE INVESTIGATED

895
00:47:11.245 --> 00:47:12.829
Do you see anything?

896
00:47:12.913 --> 00:47:14.581
You're barking up the wrong tree.

897
00:47:16.542 --> 00:47:18.835
COUNTRY PUPPETS

898
00:47:19.670 --> 00:47:21.213
There is nothing in these.

899
00:47:21.296 --> 00:47:22.339
Beyond belief.

900
00:47:26.218 --> 00:47:27.594
Wait a minute.

901
00:47:27.678 --> 00:47:29.555
It is said that Jeweler An did it.

902
00:47:30.722 --> 00:47:33.016
He came to the vault.
Is that when he killed the victim?

903
00:47:33.100 --> 00:47:34.560
JEWELER AN WENT TO THE VAULT

904
00:47:35.185 --> 00:47:39.231
We don't know, he could be lying.
-That's what he said.

905
00:47:39.314 --> 00:47:41.400
Then, I guess.
-Bong-cheon asked him here.

906
00:47:41.483 --> 00:47:45.362
From how many?
- It must have been after ten in the evening.

907
00:47:45.445 --> 00:47:49.283
The person who came here at 11 p.m
couldn't tell who was in the vault.

908
00:47:50.200 --> 00:47:52.828
I went to his study at 10:10 p.m.

909
00:47:52.911 --> 00:47:56.498
Then he asked
suddenly me too.

910
00:47:56.582 --> 00:47:59.167
I couldn't surprise him anymore.

911
00:47:59.251 --> 00:48:01.878
I gave up on the idea and left at 10:30 p.m.

912
00:48:01.962 --> 00:48:03.630
You weren't lucky either.

913
00:48:03.714 --> 00:48:06.550
Between 22:30 and 23:10 -

914
00:48:06.633 --> 00:48:09.303
the CEO was nowhere to be found.

915
00:48:09.386 --> 00:48:11.722
If he was already dead then,

916
00:48:11.805 --> 00:48:17.060
The jeweler would have had it
enough time to kill -

917
00:48:17.144 --> 00:48:20.897
and go to the vault.

918
00:48:22.399 --> 00:48:27.738
We have to piece together the story in our heads,
so we can find the killer.

919
00:48:27.821 --> 00:48:32.117
Even if your theory isn't perfect,
please explain carefully

920
00:48:32.200 --> 00:48:33.910
who do you suspect is the killer.

921
00:48:33.994 --> 00:48:39.541
The jeweler was at the top of my list,
but now I'm on stage two.

922
00:48:39.625 --> 00:48:40.626
I'll explain why.

923
00:48:40.709 --> 00:48:45.797
Merikrot's ignorance spoiled
his life and took his wife's life.

924
00:48:45.881 --> 00:48:52.429
Hence his motive
destroy us all is more believable.

925
00:48:52.512 --> 00:48:56.016
If we assume
that Mr. Kingfisher is a killer,

926
00:48:56.099 --> 00:49:00.395
how would he have gotten into the vault?
That's where the murder was committed.

927
00:49:01.229 --> 00:49:04.524
HOW DID JANG THE OCTOPUS GET INTO THE VAULT?

928
00:49:08.153 --> 00:49:09.404
That's what I remember.

929
00:49:09.488 --> 00:49:16.328
Mr. Merikrotti was always the CEO
with, when he took care of the payments.

930
00:49:16.411 --> 00:49:18.080
Mr. Merikrotiko?
-Together?

931
00:49:18.163 --> 00:49:21.583
Did he always go along?
- I saw him a couple of times.

932
00:49:21.667 --> 00:49:24.544
Where did you meet?
-In my office on the 8th.

933
00:49:24.628 --> 00:49:30.342
I realized that he could have made it
vault easily, unlike others.

934
00:49:30.425 --> 00:49:35.180
CEO Kim trusted him.
Maybe he stopped being careful.

935
00:49:35.764 --> 00:49:40.227
He said Merikrotti took the payments
With Bong-cheon to the town hall.

936
00:49:40.310 --> 00:49:44.815
You can access the City Hall archives
with the civil servant's identity card.

937
00:49:44.898 --> 00:49:47.484
Sea turtles have nimble hands.

938
00:49:47.567 --> 00:49:50.904
He is an excellent card cheat
and a master of disguise.

939
00:49:50.987 --> 00:49:54.950
He easily could have
steal someone's identity card -

940
00:49:55.033 --> 00:49:59.454
and visit regularly
reading documents at the town hall.

941
00:50:05.544 --> 00:50:09.423
I can't help it
that I doubt the Jeweler the most.

942
00:50:11.007 --> 00:50:15.554
The killer was someone who had
reason to plan a convoluted murder.

943
00:50:15.637 --> 00:50:18.807
To him, this was all symbolic.

944
00:50:18.890 --> 00:50:23.437
The killer had his reasons
want to kill us here.

945
00:50:23.520 --> 00:50:25.647
Whose motive seems the strongest?

946
00:50:27.858 --> 00:50:28.859
His.

947
00:50:29.943 --> 00:50:31.528
That's all.

948
00:50:32.279 --> 00:50:38.285
Keep in mind the motive, the evidence,
circumstances, access to the vault and alibis.

949
00:50:38.368 --> 00:50:41.538
Vote for the person
which you suspect the most.

950
00:50:42.956 --> 00:50:46.251
I still don't know.
- No idea.

951
00:50:47.127 --> 00:50:49.796
WHY DID IT HAPPEN HERE TODAY
IN THE PRESENCE OF EVERYONE?

952
00:50:51.673 --> 00:50:55.385
WHO WANTED TO BREAK THE CHAIN,
WHO HAD CONNECTED THEM FOR A LONG TIME?

953
00:50:57.846 --> 00:50:59.347
WHO IS REALLY GUILTY?

954
00:50:59.431 --> 00:51:01.016
The thugs too.

955
00:51:03.185 --> 00:51:05.228
I will die before the culprit is found.

956
00:51:05.312 --> 00:51:06.438
VOTING STARTS

957
00:51:06.521 --> 00:51:07.981
I trust my instincts.

958
00:51:11.067 --> 00:51:13.195
This was a difficult investigation.

959
00:51:13.278 --> 00:51:15.363
My mind is spinning
theories and possibilities.

960
00:51:16.740 --> 00:51:21.286
All events
trace back to the landfill.

961
00:51:21.369 --> 00:51:24.664
Instead of a landfill
Heoyoung's casino was built.

962
00:51:24.748 --> 00:51:29.669
